{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789332846,"nonce":"l/FYKhCv+WTS3+A4IACepbP4+sc=","title":"Python: a call through a lambda or nested def boxes everything","message":"`bench_lambda_call.py` (10M calls of `step = lambda acc, i: acc + i % 8`)\nand `bench_closure_call.py` (the same through a nested def capturing `k`),\n3 runs, medians:\n\n    lambda_call   zynml 12.8 ms   zypy 2188 ms   cpython 660 ms\n    closure_call  zynml n/a       zypy 3534 ms   cpython 828 ms\n\nEvery call through a function value goes through `zb_call_N`: the record\nunboxed and its arity checked, each argument boxed (an allocation each),\nthe body run on dynamic values (`zb_any_arith`), the result boxed and read\nback. 220 to 350 ns a call, three to four times slower than CPython.\n\nFix: a known-callee type `Ty::Closure(k)` for lambdas and nested defs.\nInference collects every closure before the module fixpoint, types its\nparameters from what the calls pass (as it already does for closed module\nfunctions) and its result from the body; a closure whose value reaches\nanywhere but a call, a local or a return escapes, and keeps dynamic\nparameters. Lowering emits a typed entry `\u003cname\u003e$typed(env, p: T..) -\u003e R`\nnext to the dynamic adapter the record names, and a call on a value of\ntype `Closure(k)` calls the typed entry directly. Everything else sees the\nvalue as a dynamic one.\n\nAfter (same runner):\n\n    lambda_call   zynml 13.2 ms   zypy 19.5 ms   cpython 698 ms\n    closure_call                  zypy 67.7 ms   cpython 821 ms\n\nWhat remains in the lambda loop is one `zb_unbox_list_raw_any` call whose\nresult is unused (the typed entry ignores `env` when nothing is captured,\nbut an extern call is never dead) and the pending-exception check; in the\nclosure loop, three extern box reads per iteration for the captured cell.\nBoth are the accessor-as-loads issue.","files":null}]}